From 59af2c667b2ac820baafc74b60e7f733334fe9b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:26:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: cheaper 3D texture filtering (Warzone2100$Filter);
 800x600 window by default

Terrain and model textures used trilinear filtering with 4x anisotropy.
Mesa's software rasteriser implements anisotropy with several trilinear
lookups per pixel, the slowest texture path it has. On RISC OS the new
pie_Set3DTextureFilter() uses bilinear filtering from the nearest mipmap
level and no anisotropy by default; Warzone2100$Filter = best | smooth |
fast | nearest selects upstream's filtering, trilinear, the default, or
unfiltered. Other platforms keep upstream's settings.

A desktop window now defaults to 800x600 (was 1024x768 since 0007).
